Cell["\<\
The tangent and cotangent models use adjacency or equality at each position \
of a ray. The displacement model uses this rule on the two entries of a pair. \
Their vertical graphs and transverse multiplicities depend on the substrate. \
Materializing a construction gives an ordinary literal fibered graph for the \
general readers. Supported models also have explicit predicate methods that \
materialize once, so manual conversion is optional.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d248b19a-d5d4-475a-bee2-58ffbf001139"],

Cell["\<\
The same cycle supports two ray models and a displacement model.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb5c7e2d-d26b-4ca1-aae8-6766878a682b"],

