Cell["Exact reduction by observations", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0096b820-008f-4bd4-acaa-13a4672fdb98"],

Cell["\<\
An observation map groups total vertices into classes and thereby defines \
another reconstructed base. This quotient records whether some edge joins two \
classes. It does not retain how many lifts each representative has. The \
multiplicity measurement reads that information before reduction.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8eb12039-96b7-428a-8694-f32caba3b55e"],

Cell["\<\
Here adjacent pairs of vertices of a cycle become single observed states. \
Each fiber is an edge, but its two endpoints lift different directions of the \
quotient cycle. This is a valid fibered graph without the weak fibration \
property.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"22629ad2-aa32-457f-b095-bc7d52d71967"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

